Thu Nov  5 19:55:12 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 1.23.0
  * Compile Unicode character classes in regular expressions using
   UTF-8 byte sequences for smaller and faster PikeVM code (1baf65c).
  * Add support for \b{start-half} and \b{end-half} word boundary
    assertions in regular expressions (e89aaae).
  * Auto-discover libmagic library search path when building with
    the magic-module feature (64dd140).
  * BUGFIX: Allow --ignore-module to ignore modules implemented by
    YARA-X (#833).
  * BUGFIX: Don't mistake maps containing encoding and value keys
    for encoded values in the Python API (#832).
  * BUGFIX: Fix memory leaks in the Go API when Destroy isn't
    called on Scanner or Rules (c465b46).
  * BUGFIX: Fix false positive E048 (ConditionTooLarge) errors
    when multiple rules share a WASM function (71cfcc9).
  * BUGFIX: Support regular expressions in with statements without
    panicking (6b7bbb7).
  * BUGFIX: Handle literal null bytes in metadata strings without
    panicking (c557033, d970018).
  * BUGFIX: Fix overlapping undefined-variable bitmaps in WASM
    memory when rules use more than 8 variables (2fcf36e).
  * BUGFIX: Roll back anchored_sub_patterns when restoring
    compiler snapshots after a rule fails to compile (e2153a9).
  * BUGFIX: Fix multiple loop hoisting and variable stack issues in
    the compiler (3b09b1e, 1cdf204, a2a4823, 0165856, 14ec84b).
  * BUGFIX: Fix panics, integer overflows, and excessive memory
    usage when compiling large patterns, wide patterns, hex jumps,
    and multi-pattern regex sets (f2fa044, ac2e94b, 7883874,
    294a49a, c46e2a7, 0f71e3b, eed7687).
  * BUGFIX: Fix panics, infinite loops, and error span mapping in
    relaxed_re_syntax mode (64c2a16, 431834f, e3a6a23, 95cd52e,
    fb2332a).
  * BUGFIX: Fix stack overflows on deeply nested expressions, span
    overflows on large inputs, and Unicode whitespace handling in
    parser and formatter (9e89546, 9137a19, 64d4d90, b107e9d,
    985d3cd, 46ea1af, c7d4afb, 24d964f).
  * BUGFIX: Fix integer overflows, 32-bit offset truncation, WASM
    page boundary slices, and large runtime string handling in
    compiler and scanner (02c6d37, 3af8e05, 852fed0, 77d84c8).
  * BUGFIX: Fix arithmetic overflows and panics on unset fields in
    math, hash, console, and pe modules (e7510e2, 220a268, 30074ca,
    8001188, 8f4999a).
  * BUGFIX: Fix panics and unbounded recursion in yr check, yr deps,
    yr fix warnings, and the tags linter (360f42f, d90d431, b2293bd,
    f489e2d).
  * BUGFIX: Fix multiple issues in the Language Server, including
    unbounded recursion, lexical scoping in find_declaration, UTF-16
    column mapping, and stale CST caching (2c0360c, b4b9192, 5a1c488,
    8b6d7f1, 1973e8a, b3e1ffe).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 26 19:43:57 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 1.22.1
  * BUGFIX: panic when a regex is translated to a masked literal
    and it has the fullword modifier (a0b49a4).
  * BUGFIX: panic when compiling regexes with deeply nested fixed
    repetitions (834e697).
- Update to version 1.22.0
  * Add int64, int64be, uint64, and uint64be built-in functions,
    and support for unsigned 64-bit integers and integer literals.
    greater than i64::MAX (#806).
  * Add pe.offset_to_rva function to pe module to convert file
    offsets to RVAs (07f7a94).
  * Keep the width and signedness of protobuf integer fields (#806)
  * Implement constant folding for integer division and modulus
    operations (#806).
  * Raise warnings on implicit sign conversions that change
    constant values and unary operations on unsigned integers
    (#806).
  * Allow the yr dump command to show information from the zip
    module (3bbe876).
  * Link compiler errors and warnings to their documentation
    pages (d34819c).
  * Expose xor_key for matching patterns in the C and Go APIs
    (#814).
  * Performance and memory consumption improvements (#808, #810,
    9c2b3c7).
  * Improve Language Server with Workspace Symbols support, better
    Code Completion documentation, auto-importing modules on
    non-top-level symbol completion, and --help/--version CLI flags
    (#788, #792, #795, #797, #798).
  * Improve documentation for math.entropy function (#783).
  * BUGFIX: Limit the size of emitted WASM functions and return
    error when a rule condition is too large (#813).
  * BUGFIX: Don't force yara-x default features in yara-x-capi
    (#802).
  * BUGFIX: Avoid WASM trap when dividing i64::MIN by -1
    (7d16c1f).
  * BUGFIX: Ensure quantifiers computed at runtime that are out of
    range are never satisfied (af690da).
  * BUGFIX: Dix the number of iterations in loops over ranges when
    bounds overflow (697e36e).
  * BUGFIX: Don't truncate 64-bit offsets and indexes on 32-bit
    platforms (9e00369).
  * BUGFIX: Improve robustness of deserialized rule data validation
    (9d6a1d8).
  * BUGFIX: Enhance C API robustness with comprehensive null checks
    and detailed error reporting (0ed7485).
  * BUGFIX: Correct output line termination when progress bar is
    active in yr scan (029e9c9).

